 testl)

emit_int_cmp_impl and emit_fused_cmp_branch_impl staged EVERY rhs in
%ecx, so a constant compare cost 8 bytes:
    movl $36, %ecx ; cmpl %ecx, %eax
where GCC emits 3..6:
    cmpl $36, %eax          (testl %eax,%eax for C==0, 2 bytes)
testl is flag-identical to cmpl $0 for every Jcc (both clear CF/OF,
set SF/ZF/PF from eax). Bonus: %ecx stays untouched across constant
compares, removing a false dependency the peephole had to clean up.

